WEBVTT

00:00:14.513 --> 00:00:16.863
&lt;i&gt;RANSOM: The&lt;/i&gt;Cerritos &lt;i&gt;is
in orbit around Beta III.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:16.907 --> 00:00:18.430
&lt;i&gt;Back in the day,
these guys worshipped&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:18.474 --> 00:00:20.737
&lt;i&gt;a violent god
called Landru, who suppressed&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.347
&lt;i&gt;their creativity
and made them kill each other,&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:22.391 --> 00:00:24.262
&lt;i&gt;until Kirk figured out
it was actually a computer.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:24.306 --> 00:00:25.524
&lt;i&gt;Get this.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:25.568 --> 00:00:27.352
&lt;i&gt;At some point,
these knuckleheads went&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:27.396 --> 00:00:29.093
&lt;i&gt;back to worshipping Landru.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:29.137 --> 00:00:30.225
&lt;i&gt;Captain Freeman has been&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:30.268 --> 00:00:31.878
&lt;i&gt;setting them straight
all morning.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:31.922 --> 00:00:33.358
I can't believe you all started

00:00:33.402 --> 00:00:35.230
re-worshipping
the dang computer.

00:00:35.273 --> 00:00:37.101
Well, Landru's very persuasive.

00:00:37.145 --> 00:00:39.495
&lt;i&gt;LANDRU:
Consume the intruders! &lt;i&gt;
Obey Landru!&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:39.538 --> 00:00:42.889
Hey, don't make me paradox you
into destroying yourself.

00:00:42.933 --> 00:00:45.327
&lt;i&gt;LANDRU:
Landru apologizes.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:47.329
[groans] This is literally
the exact thing

00:00:47.372 --> 00:00:48.939
Captain Kirk taught you.

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:50.897
Maybe write it down this time?

00:00:50.941 --> 00:00:54.423
&lt;i&gt;Cerritos,&lt;/i&gt;two to beam up.

00:00:54.466 --> 00:00:56.555
Well, I like purging people
during the red hour.

00:00:56.599 --> 00:00:58.122
I'm going to keep doing it.

00:00:58.166 --> 00:00:59.863
Dude, there is
no more red hour, okay?

00:00:59.906 --> 00:01:02.431
-Let it go.-But I just bought a new scythe.

00:01:05.477 --> 00:01:07.044
Ugh, Landru.

00:01:07.088 --> 00:01:09.481
I know, it's always weird
revisiting planets

00:01:09.525 --> 00:01:11.266
-from the TOS era.
-TOS?

00:01:11.309 --> 00:01:13.006
It's what I call the 2260s.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:15.792
Stands for "those old
scientists"-- you know, Spock,

00:01:15.835 --> 00:01:18.229
Scotty, those guys.
Seems like they were stumbling

00:01:18.273 --> 00:01:21.972
on crazy new aliens
every week back then.

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:24.061
Nothing against
second contact missions,

00:01:24.105 --> 00:01:26.281
but the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos
should be popping in&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:26.324 --> 00:01:29.066
on those legacy civilizations &lt;i&gt;
before&lt;/i&gt;they unravel.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:31.112
Yeah, but "popping in" is
against regulation.

00:01:31.155 --> 00:01:32.896
We would need specific orders.

00:01:32.939 --> 00:01:35.159
I just hate seeing a perfectly
good society get destroyed

00:01:35.203 --> 00:01:37.422
by a Gamester of Triskelion
or whatever,

00:01:37.466 --> 00:01:40.382
because Starfleet has a policy
of &lt;i&gt;some&lt;/i&gt;intervention.

00:01:41.948 --> 00:01:44.995
-Set coordinates
for Starbase 77.
-Sorry, Captain,

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:47.258
but we still have crew
on Beta III.

00:01:47.302 --> 00:01:49.130
I didn't authorize that.
Who is it?

00:01:49.173 --> 00:01:51.523
Art supplies!
Get your art supplies!

00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:53.134
We got paints,
we got brushes,

00:01:53.177 --> 00:01:55.266
we got a spiky, pencil,
twirl-around thingy.

00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:57.268
Boost your creativity!
Express yourself!

00:01:57.312 --> 00:01:59.531
Stop praying to a computer!

00:01:59.575 --> 00:02:02.099
Hoo boy,
incoming lecture in five,

00:02:02.143 --> 00:02:03.274
four...

00:02:03.318 --> 00:02:04.841
Who wants crayons?
Here you go, kid.

00:02:04.884 --> 00:02:06.103
Way better than the red hour.

00:02:06.147 --> 00:02:07.887
Since when
do you break protocol?

00:02:07.931 --> 00:02:09.541
I'm just tired of you getting
to do all the good stuff

00:02:09.585 --> 00:02:11.064
while I stick to the rules.

00:02:11.108 --> 00:02:12.196
&lt;i&gt;RANSOM:
Ensign Boimler? Do you read?&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:13.415
Whoa-ho-ho,

00:02:13.458 --> 00:02:15.330
look at Brad Boimler
being cool for once.

00:02:15.373 --> 00:02:17.462
[gasps] Wait, is this
because of my teachings?

00:02:17.506 --> 00:02:20.030
Okay, you don't teach.
You just instigate chaos.

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:22.989
Exactly-- helpful,
character-building chaos.

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:24.382
&lt;i&gt;RANSOM: I can hear you, can you hear me?&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:24.426 --> 00:02:25.992
&lt;i&gt;MARINER: Aw, Boims!
I thought you were gonna&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:26.036 --> 00:02:27.472
&lt;i&gt;get stuck
in middle management,&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:27.516 --> 00:02:30.214
like this pathetic
little fly in amber, like--

00:02:30.258 --> 00:02:33.086
&lt;i&gt;-Oh, like Ransom!-I am not a little fly in amber!&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:35.176
What did it, huh?
My constant mockery?

00:02:35.219 --> 00:02:38.483
My non-stop prodding?
My downright-dangerous hazing?

00:02:38.527 --> 00:02:40.093
No, no. Look.

00:02:40.137 --> 00:02:42.139
If you have to know,
I found out about your secret.

00:02:42.183 --> 00:02:44.141
You mean never eating after
7:00? it's a miracle, right?

00:02:44.185 --> 00:02:46.491
-I mean, it does work,
you should try it.
-Captain Freeman is your mom.

00:02:46.535 --> 00:02:48.406
Yeah, I don't, I don't know
what you're talking about.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:50.626
Oh, come on, Mariner.
The captain's your mom.

00:02:50.669 --> 00:02:52.018
&lt;i&gt;Your dad's an admiral.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:52.062 --> 00:02:53.498
&lt;i&gt;You're basically
Starfleet royalty.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:53.542 --> 00:02:54.978
&lt;i&gt;How cool is that?&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:55.021 --> 00:02:56.327
Shut the [bleep] up right now,
Boimler.

00:02:56.371 --> 00:02:58.286
-Shut your [bleep] mouth.
-This is a good thing!

00:02:58.329 --> 00:03:00.679
Now we can both do some good
and you'll just, you know,

00:03:00.723 --> 00:03:02.290
&lt;i&gt;keep us out of trouble
with your mom--&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:02.333 --> 00:03:04.292
&lt;i&gt;-What?! No that is not how--
-I just don't understand&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:04.335 --> 00:03:06.511
&lt;i&gt;-why it's such a secret.
I'd be telling everyone.
-Move!&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:06.555 --> 00:03:08.600
Dude, I do not want people
knowing my mom is my mom!

00:03:08.644 --> 00:03:10.515
Okay, okay.
I'm not gonna tell a soul.

00:03:10.559 --> 00:03:12.038
I'm being serious! Shut up!

00:03:12.082 --> 00:03:14.519
So, uh, does Captain Mommy
give you,

00:03:14.563 --> 00:03:17.043
uh, sweet little captain kisses?

00:03:17.087 --> 00:03:19.394
[smooching]

00:03:19.437 --> 00:03:21.222
[screaming]

00:04:29.681 --> 00:04:31.683
♪

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:45.088
-Plasma ring scan is complete,
Captain Dayton.
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:45.131 --> 00:04:46.742
I loved the &lt;i&gt;Rubidoux&lt;/i&gt;,
but nothing beats

00:04:46.785 --> 00:04:48.744
a brand new ship-- hey!

00:04:48.787 --> 00:04:50.572
Who peeled this film
off the weapons panel?!

00:04:50.615 --> 00:04:52.617
Come on, guys!

00:04:52.661 --> 00:04:56.360
I want the &lt;i&gt;Solvang&lt;/i&gt;to beperfect for as long as possible.

00:04:56.404 --> 00:04:58.841
Hey! Take those shoes
off right now!

00:05:00.538 --> 00:05:02.192
What?

00:05:03.324 --> 00:05:06.152
-Aah! What the hell was that?!
-We're being fired upon.

00:05:06.196 --> 00:05:08.372
-Raise shield, red alert.
-Get us out of here!

00:05:10.374 --> 00:05:13.334
Shields at ten percent.

00:05:14.552 --> 00:05:16.249
Direct hit to main engines.

00:05:18.513 --> 00:05:20.471
-[alarm sounding]
-Warp! Now!

00:05:30.089 --> 00:05:31.613
Ah! I can't believe I get

00:05:31.656 --> 00:05:32.918
to be orientation liaison
for a new recruit.

00:05:32.962 --> 00:05:35.094
I am going
to show her so many ropes.

00:05:35.138 --> 00:05:36.879
Hello? Rutherford?

00:05:36.922 --> 00:05:38.750
Sorry. Just trying
to adjust this little thingy

00:05:38.794 --> 00:05:41.013
on my implant's
attitude selector.

00:05:41.057 --> 00:05:42.928
Crazy about Mariner
and the captain, right?

00:05:42.972 --> 00:05:44.539
Oh, man, Captain Freeman Day

00:05:44.582 --> 00:05:46.062
is gonna be super awkward
this year.

00:05:46.105 --> 00:05:47.672
-[both yell]
-There's the shuttle!

00:05:47.716 --> 00:05:50.109
Huh. Look at this new button!

00:05:50.153 --> 00:05:53.069
Optimistic mode?
This is going to be great!

00:05:53.112 --> 00:05:55.288
But... sexy mode? Mmm.

00:05:55.332 --> 00:05:57.247
Don't mind if I do.
[laughs]

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:59.989
[English accent]:
'Ello. Chim chimurri.
What's all this then?

00:06:04.123 --> 00:06:07.953
[whirring, trilling]

00:06:07.997 --> 00:06:09.607
Aw, it's beautiful!

00:06:09.651 --> 00:06:12.088
Oh, there she is--
the little robot exocomp!

00:06:12.131 --> 00:06:13.959
Oh, my gosh. Hi.
Are you Ensign Tendi?

00:06:14.003 --> 00:06:16.266
Oh, my gosh. Yes, I am!
And I'm so happy you're here!

00:06:16.309 --> 00:06:18.964
I'm happy to &lt;i&gt;be&lt;/i&gt;here!
[laughs] This is so exciting!

00:06:19.008 --> 00:06:21.619
Ooh-wee! Howdy there.
Now I'm talking like a cowboy.

00:06:21.663 --> 00:06:24.666
-That was a weird thing to say!
-It sure was!

00:06:24.709 --> 00:06:27.582
Ugh. Why did we ever keep this
a secret in the first place?

00:06:27.625 --> 00:06:29.975
Ugh! I just wanted to fly
under the radar!

00:06:30.019 --> 00:06:31.934
And I didn't want anyone to knowthe most demerited officer

00:06:31.977 --> 00:06:33.979
in the fleet was my daughter.

00:06:34.023 --> 00:06:35.807
Well, Wesley Crusher worked
with his mom.

00:06:35.851 --> 00:06:37.330
Maybe
everybody'll be cool about it.

00:06:37.374 --> 00:06:39.898
Captain, captain's daughter...
Uh, I mean Mariner.

00:06:39.942 --> 00:06:41.160
Oh, what is it, Jack?

00:06:41.204 --> 00:06:43.032
Captain,
I'm putting together a list

00:06:43.075 --> 00:06:44.860
of candidates
for the &lt;i&gt;Sacramento&lt;/i&gt;promotion.

00:06:44.903 --> 00:06:47.602
I'd love your input.
May I just say

00:06:47.645 --> 00:06:50.300
I am very sorry
if I ever treated you

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:52.302
with anything other
than admiration.

00:06:52.345 --> 00:06:54.652
Oh, shut up, Ransom!
You're such a suck-up!

00:06:54.696 --> 00:06:57.699
From now on, I'll make sure
to give you special attention.

00:06:57.742 --> 00:07:00.005
No! Be as hard on her
as you always are!

00:07:00.049 --> 00:07:02.007
-Yeah, be hard on me!
-I'm only hard on you

00:07:02.051 --> 00:07:03.748
when you make me hard! I mean,
I'm-I'm not hard right now!

00:07:03.792 --> 00:07:06.185
I mean, I could... I could
get hard, if I wanted to,

00:07:06.229 --> 00:07:08.710
but I'm not hard right now.I'm so sorry! You're both great!

00:07:08.753 --> 00:07:10.755
Ugh!

00:07:14.063 --> 00:07:15.760
I heard
she's the captain's daughter.

00:07:15.804 --> 00:07:19.024
[indistinct whispering]

00:07:19.068 --> 00:07:21.636
Hey, Mariner,
I'm Lieutenant Levy.

00:07:21.679 --> 00:07:23.681
We went on a date last year.
I don't know if you recall.

00:07:23.725 --> 00:07:25.030
Yeah, Steve, I remember.

00:07:25.074 --> 00:07:27.642
You said
Wolf 359 was an inside job.

00:07:27.685 --> 00:07:30.209
[laughing]: It totally was.
So, hey, I was wondering,

00:07:30.253 --> 00:07:32.168
could give this
to your mom for me?

00:07:32.211 --> 00:07:34.083
It's just a few ideas I threw
together on how to decorate

00:07:34.126 --> 00:07:35.780
-the captain's yacht.
-Fine. Whatever.

00:07:35.824 --> 00:07:37.695
You're the best.
Thanks, Mariner.

00:07:37.739 --> 00:07:39.392
Changelings aren't real.
The Dominion War didn't happen!

00:07:39.436 --> 00:07:41.569
-Hey, Mariner!
Okay, can you just?
-[groaning]

00:07:41.612 --> 00:07:43.353
-Oh, okay, little closer.-Hey, don't log that, all right?

00:07:43.396 --> 00:07:45.224
-I don't want
to see that up on the... Oh!
-Hey!

00:07:45.268 --> 00:07:47.357
This is a service corridor,
not a social club, Ensign.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.098
Sorry, Doc. Won't happen again.

00:07:49.141 --> 00:07:50.839
You think
your mom would be okay

00:07:50.882 --> 00:07:53.015
with me and Shaxs making
a little love connection?

00:07:53.058 --> 00:07:57.019
I'd love to snag that Bajoran
beefsteak with my coital hooks.

00:07:57.062 --> 00:07:59.108
Captain, we've received
a partial distress call

00:07:59.151 --> 00:08:00.718
from the &lt;i&gt;Solvang.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:00.762 --> 00:08:02.241
I guess Captain Dayton's
still getting used

00:08:02.285 --> 00:08:04.069
to the controls in her new ship.

00:08:04.113 --> 00:08:06.419
Sir, the signal originated
in the Kalla system.

00:08:06.463 --> 00:08:08.247
Well, there isn't anything
distressing there.

00:08:08.291 --> 00:08:09.945
The &lt;i&gt;Titan&lt;/i&gt;is also within range.

00:08:09.988 --> 00:08:12.077
No. Let them know
that we have it. [laughs]

00:08:12.121 --> 00:08:14.036
Dayton's going to hate
that we came running

00:08:14.079 --> 00:08:16.778
to her rescue because
someone leaned on a button.

00:08:19.302 --> 00:08:22.174
-[grunting]
-Oh, this sucks.

00:08:22.218 --> 00:08:24.263
Yo, yo, Mariner!

00:08:24.307 --> 00:08:26.614
I was just crossing
through the, um, lower decks,

00:08:26.657 --> 00:08:28.659
and I replicated you
some hand pies.

00:08:28.703 --> 00:08:31.140
Hand... What is a hand pie?
You know what? No thank you.

00:08:31.183 --> 00:08:33.272
-Ooh, key lime? Mmm. Mmm.
-I won't be able

00:08:33.316 --> 00:08:35.884
to do any of my usual
sneaky Robin Hood stuff

00:08:35.927 --> 00:08:37.276
now that everybody's
paying attention to me.

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:39.235
Yesterday, he literally
didn't know my name.

00:08:39.278 --> 00:08:41.759
He called me "Jen."
Who here is named "Jen"?!

00:08:41.803 --> 00:08:44.196
Ugh. You are so right. He was
clearly kissing your butt.

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:46.111
It's not like
he had a prewritten letter

00:08:46.155 --> 00:08:47.809
of recommendation which would
save you so much time

00:08:47.852 --> 00:08:49.288
since all you had
to do is sign it.

00:08:49.332 --> 00:08:51.813
-Oh, Boimler, not you!
-Ransom's picking someone

00:08:51.856 --> 00:08:53.292
to promote to the &lt;i&gt;Sacramento.
I need an edge!&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:53.336 --> 00:08:55.207
Dude, I thought
you were done being lame!

00:08:55.251 --> 00:08:57.819
Yeah, but it's the &lt;i&gt;Sac.
That's a huge career boost!&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:57.862 --> 00:08:59.864
And didn't you say you'd get me
in a captain's chair?

00:08:59.908 --> 00:09:01.431
Mariner!
Looking good, girlfriend!

00:09:01.474 --> 00:09:03.172
Get phased, Lundy.

00:09:03.215 --> 00:09:05.653
Wait. No one would know me
on the &lt;i&gt;Sacramento.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:05.696 --> 00:09:07.393
I'd be a nobody again,
like you!

00:09:07.437 --> 00:09:09.178
I'm not a nobody. I...

00:09:09.221 --> 00:09:10.745
Maybe &lt;i&gt;I&lt;/i&gt;should apply
to the &lt;i&gt;Sacramento.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:10.788 --> 00:09:12.137
I don't know.
They might be looking

00:09:12.181 --> 00:09:14.052
for someone a little less
criminally insubordinate.

00:09:14.096 --> 00:09:16.707
Good call. I'd better start
adjusting my attitude, sir.

00:09:16.751 --> 00:09:18.317
-Ew. Don't call me "sir."
-Yes, sir.

00:09:18.361 --> 00:09:20.015
-Don't.
-You technically
outrank me, sir.

00:09:20.058 --> 00:09:21.886
-BOIMLER: What are you doing?
Stop it.
-Is that an order?

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:23.975
-BOIMLER: Yes. I mean, no.
-Permission to go
to my station, sir?

00:09:24.019 --> 00:09:27.152
-You have a station?
-Ha-ha! Good one, sir. Mm-hmm.

00:09:27.196 --> 00:09:28.763
Nobody's gonna fall for that.

00:09:28.806 --> 00:09:30.155
-[yelps]
-I want to give Mariner
a present!

00:09:30.199 --> 00:09:31.679
That's a processing hub,

00:09:31.722 --> 00:09:34.159
and that's a pattern-buffer
maintenance hatch.

00:09:34.203 --> 00:09:36.379
So, hey, um, do you want me
to call you "Exocomp,"

00:09:36.422 --> 00:09:37.946
or do you have
an alpha-numeric name,

00:09:37.989 --> 00:09:41.297
like TT30311?

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:43.255
[scoffs] No.
I didn't want to sound robotic.

00:09:43.299 --> 00:09:45.127
I wanted to be called
something normal,

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:47.172
so I analyzed
all Federation languages

00:09:47.216 --> 00:09:50.306
and calculated
a mathematically perfect name.

00:09:50.349 --> 00:09:52.308
-What is it?
-Peanut Hamper.

00:09:52.351 --> 00:09:53.831
Peanut Hamper?

00:09:53.875 --> 00:09:55.920
I love it!

00:09:55.964 --> 00:09:57.748
♪

00:09:57.792 --> 00:09:59.750
Heading
to Commander Ransom's office?

00:09:59.794 --> 00:10:01.404
-Cut it out.
-Cut what out, sir?

00:10:01.447 --> 00:10:03.319
I'm heading there as well,
to explain

00:10:03.362 --> 00:10:05.103
why I should be promoted
over to the &lt;i&gt;Sacramento.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:05.147 --> 00:10:06.844
You know,Ransom's not just some meathead.

00:10:06.888 --> 00:10:08.541
He's gonna see
right through you.

00:10:08.585 --> 00:10:10.543
Boimler,
your record is spotless.

00:10:10.587 --> 00:10:12.110
It's freaky.

00:10:12.154 --> 00:10:13.851
Thank you, sir.
There is more on the back.

00:10:13.895 --> 00:10:16.854
On the other hand, Mariner &lt;i&gt;is
the captain's daughter.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:16.898 --> 00:10:18.073
Mm, sort of stuck
between a rock

00:10:18.116 --> 00:10:19.335
and a kiss-ass place,
aren't we, sir?

00:10:19.378 --> 00:10:21.032
[groans]
Boimler, you're so promotable,

00:10:21.076 --> 00:10:23.034
but I live to serve the captain.

00:10:23.078 --> 00:10:24.862
[frustrated grunt]
I can't think until I work out.

00:10:24.906 --> 00:10:26.342
You've been lifting
this whole time.

00:10:26.385 --> 00:10:27.386
Get out of here!

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:30.085
I'm trying to think...!

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:32.870
Ooh!

00:10:32.914 --> 00:10:34.437
[chuckles]:
Hmm, dilithium.

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:35.960
It's better than I thought.

00:10:36.004 --> 00:10:38.354
Dang it!
Aw, shoot. Ooh, ooh.

00:10:38.397 --> 00:10:40.835
[chuckles]: Sorry.Ensign Klutz reporting for duty.

00:10:40.878 --> 00:10:42.837
Ah, Peanut Hamper is such
an innocent little robot.

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:44.795
I got to make sure
she doesn't get overwhelmed

00:10:44.839 --> 00:10:46.797
during our shift, you know,
since she doesn't have

00:10:46.841 --> 00:10:48.407
-any hands.
-With you watching out for her,

00:10:48.451 --> 00:10:51.062
-I'm sure she'll do great.
-Whoa. Are you mad at me?

00:10:51.106 --> 00:10:53.891
I just think that Dr. T'ana's
going to be mean, and...

00:10:53.935 --> 00:10:55.893
[yawns]: I'm not.
I'm just trying to click

00:10:55.937 --> 00:10:59.505
this attitude button
until I get back to normal.

00:10:59.549 --> 00:11:01.116
Just make sure
you treat Peanut Hamper

00:11:01.159 --> 00:11:03.422
the same as you would
anyone else. [gasps]

00:11:03.466 --> 00:11:05.120
-TENDI: But she's
not like anyone else.
-[giggles] Oopsy-daisy.

00:11:05.163 --> 00:11:07.339
She's been trying to pick
those tubes up this whole time.

00:11:07.383 --> 00:11:10.125
-How's she supposed to do
medical stuff?
-Oh! Dang it!

00:11:10.168 --> 00:11:11.561
T'ANA: All right,
here comes the messy part.

00:11:11.604 --> 00:11:14.564
Any slight error here
can result in instant death.

00:11:14.607 --> 00:11:17.262
Um, Dr. T'ana, just a heads-up
that Peanut Hamper might have

00:11:17.306 --> 00:11:20.091
-a little bit of trouble with...-[low buzzing]

00:11:21.092 --> 00:11:22.920
Oh. Oh, wow.

00:11:22.964 --> 00:11:25.227
Peanut Hamper, this is
some of the best micro-suturing

00:11:25.270 --> 00:11:26.794
I've ever seen.

00:11:26.837 --> 00:11:29.100
I downloaded all your journal
articles. I learned a lot.

00:11:29.144 --> 00:11:31.146
Oh, I-I could help you
With that leg if you want.

00:11:31.189 --> 00:11:32.800
Tendi, hang back.
I don't want you to get

00:11:32.843 --> 00:11:34.976
in Peanut Hamper's way.Ooh. What did you just do there?

00:11:35.019 --> 00:11:36.673
It's a new skin graft technique
I've been developing.

00:11:36.717 --> 00:11:39.371
-It uses half the skin.
-Oh, can you show me
how to do it?

00:11:39.415 --> 00:11:41.504
-TENDI: Can I... can I see?-Yeah, look at that right there.

00:11:41.547 --> 00:11:43.462
See how the flesh
just folds together?

00:11:43.506 --> 00:11:44.986
T'ANA:
[bleep]-A I do!

00:11:45.029 --> 00:11:47.031
Wow. Doc is really taking
to Peanut Hamper.

00:11:47.075 --> 00:11:49.425
Hey, don't worry. I'm sure
you'll still have a lot to do.

00:11:49.468 --> 00:11:51.470
I mean, for example, you know,
we could start working on me,

00:11:51.514 --> 00:11:53.124
getting me back up on my feet.

00:11:53.168 --> 00:11:54.517
Worry? I'm her liaison.

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:57.520
Peanut Hamper fitting in is
my greatest victory!

00:11:57.563 --> 00:11:59.217
Meld that flesh, girl!

00:11:59.261 --> 00:12:01.132
Melding away!
[giggles]

00:12:01.176 --> 00:12:04.483
Ah. "Tips for Remaining
Starfleet Uniform Compliant."

00:12:04.527 --> 00:12:05.658
The &lt;i&gt;Starfleet Manual?
Who are you kidding?&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:05.702 --> 00:12:07.138
It is so messed up
that you're trying

00:12:07.182 --> 00:12:08.531
to cheat me out of a promotion.

00:12:08.574 --> 00:12:10.315
How am I cheating?
You're always

00:12:10.359 --> 00:12:11.360
telling me to be like this.

00:12:11.403 --> 00:12:13.318
I meant to actually try
sometimes!

00:12:13.362 --> 00:12:16.060
-Not to profit off of nepotism.
-Nobody would know
Freeman's my mom

00:12:16.104 --> 00:12:17.975
if you hadn't ratted me out,

00:12:18.019 --> 00:12:19.890
so why don't you go ahead
and blame yourself?

00:12:19.934 --> 00:12:22.066
-No! I blame you!
-And I blame you right back!

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:24.373
♪

00:12:24.416 --> 00:12:25.374
Red alert.

00:12:25.417 --> 00:12:26.375
&lt;i&gt;Shields up.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:26.418 --> 00:12:27.855
[grunting]

00:12:27.898 --> 00:12:29.291
[explosion]

00:12:31.119 --> 00:12:34.078
Collision alert. Impacts
on Decks Three, 15 and 20.

00:12:34.122 --> 00:12:36.994
-My God! Is that the &lt;i&gt;Solvang?
-RANSOM: I'm not reading
any life signs.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:37.038 --> 00:12:39.040
The whole crew,
they've been wiped out.

00:12:42.957 --> 00:12:44.567
They're harvesting the wreckage!

00:12:47.004 --> 00:12:47.700
Evasive maneuvers.

00:12:52.401 --> 00:12:55.317
-Shields at 50%.
-Send out a distress call,

00:12:55.360 --> 00:12:57.014
-all frequencies.-They're jamming communications.

00:13:01.192 --> 00:13:02.715
&lt;i&gt;SHAXS: Captain, they've
latched onto the port nacelle&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:02.759 --> 00:13:04.195
&lt;i&gt;with some sort of mining arm.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:04.239 --> 00:13:06.545
-Go to warp. Get us out of here!-No! Shut down engines.

00:13:06.589 --> 00:13:08.330
But we'll be sitting ducks.

00:13:08.373 --> 00:13:09.679
Dayton would have thought
the same thing,

00:13:09.722 --> 00:13:12.160
and look what happened to them.
Shut it down!

00:13:13.944 --> 00:13:15.076
[all yelling]

00:13:30.308 --> 00:13:31.396
[both gasp]

00:13:31.440 --> 00:13:33.137
MARINER:
Mom!

00:13:33.181 --> 00:13:34.312
I-I'm okay.

00:13:34.356 --> 00:13:36.488
Auxiliary power back online.

00:13:36.532 --> 00:13:40.536
&lt;i&gt;Ha-ha-ha! I thought
theEnterprise was strong.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:40.579 --> 00:13:42.581
We &lt;i&gt;are strong.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:42.625 --> 00:13:44.888
This isn't the &lt;i&gt;Enterprise.
This is the Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:44.932 --> 00:13:48.370
&lt;i&gt;We thought you were
theEnterprise.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:48.413 --> 00:13:50.589
Pakleds?
What the hell do you want?

00:13:50.633 --> 00:13:54.419
We want your ship pieces
to add to our ship pieces,

00:13:54.463 --> 00:13:56.944
so that we have
all the ship pieces!

00:13:56.987 --> 00:13:59.598
Look, just stop this senseless
attack, and let's discuss...

00:13:59.642 --> 00:14:01.905
&lt;i&gt;JACKABOG:
No!&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:01.949 --> 00:14:03.428
&lt;i&gt;No.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:03.472 --> 00:14:04.952
We are strong!

00:14:04.995 --> 00:14:06.910
We will cut your ship apart!

00:14:06.954 --> 00:14:08.912
[groans]
This doesn't make any sense.

00:14:08.956 --> 00:14:10.609
The Pakleds aren't
this powerful.

00:14:10.653 --> 00:14:12.568
I thought
they were kind of a joke.

00:14:12.611 --> 00:14:13.830
Yeah, you guys aren't wrong.

00:14:13.874 --> 00:14:14.918
Pakleds would fake
distress calls

00:14:14.962 --> 00:14:16.659
so they could steal technology

00:14:16.702 --> 00:14:18.487
from anyone who showed up
to help, but I'm detecting

00:14:18.530 --> 00:14:20.793
weapons from over
30 different species.

00:14:20.837 --> 00:14:22.970
Ah, looks like
they're not a joke anymore.

00:14:32.805 --> 00:14:36.418
[screaming]

00:14:36.461 --> 00:14:39.856
-They're phasering the hull!
-Carving us up like
a First Contact Day salmon.

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:42.946
No engines, no weapons, fightingan enemy we don't understand.

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:44.817
We're out of options!

00:14:44.861 --> 00:14:47.559
Then I need someone
to make me some.

00:14:47.603 --> 00:14:49.953
Me? What am &lt;i&gt;I&lt;/i&gt;supposed to do?
I-I don't know these guys.

00:14:49.997 --> 00:14:51.346
Do what you do best.

00:14:51.389 --> 00:14:53.348
I need a dangerous,
half-baked solution

00:14:53.391 --> 00:14:56.655
that breaks Starfleet codes
and totally pisses me off.

00:14:56.699 --> 00:14:59.615
-[alert blaring]
-That's an order.

00:14:59.658 --> 00:15:02.661
-Boimler, what kind of computer
systems do the Pakleds use?
-They steal components

00:15:02.705 --> 00:15:04.228
from other cultures,
which means their code base

00:15:04.272 --> 00:15:05.926
-would have to be wide open.
-You catch that, Rutherford?

00:15:05.969 --> 00:15:09.625
We need a virus that takes
advantage of a trusting system!

00:15:09.668 --> 00:15:11.540
&lt;i&gt;MARINER: Exactly.
Wait, why are you so chipper?&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:11.583 --> 00:15:12.845
Implant stuff!

00:15:12.889 --> 00:15:14.673
They've got us outgunned,
and they know it.

00:15:14.717 --> 00:15:15.892
&lt;i&gt;But&lt;/i&gt;they're taking their time.

00:15:15.936 --> 00:15:17.807
If we can plant a virus
in their system,

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:20.853
-we can cripple their ship.
-Who here could whip up
a code like that?

00:15:20.897 --> 00:15:23.508
They'd have to be some sort
of morally bankrupt genius.

00:15:23.552 --> 00:15:26.468
Ha-ha! Computer, start program
Rutherford Training Beta 2.5.

00:15:26.511 --> 00:15:28.470
Can I teach you a lesson?

00:15:28.513 --> 00:15:31.516
[chuckles] Badgey! I need you
to code a virus for me.

00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:33.997
Hmm, to do that, I would needyou to disable safety protocols.

00:15:34.041 --> 00:15:35.520
[chuckles]
Wait.

00:15:35.564 --> 00:15:37.479
You're not gonna try
to kill me again, are you?

00:15:37.522 --> 00:15:38.828
Ha-ha! I'm Badgey!

00:15:38.871 --> 00:15:40.482
[chuckles nervously]
Uh, fine.

00:15:40.525 --> 00:15:42.527
Computer,
disable safety protocols.

00:15:42.571 --> 00:15:45.574
Oh, yeah!
There we go.

00:15:45.617 --> 00:15:46.705
Hello, Father.

00:15:46.749 --> 00:15:48.533
I've already created
three viruses

00:15:48.577 --> 00:15:50.622
that would disable
Pakled technology.

00:15:50.666 --> 00:15:51.841
You were monitoring comms?

00:15:51.884 --> 00:15:53.799
Oh, I'm always monitoring comms.

00:15:53.843 --> 00:15:56.759
-The packet needs
to be input manually.
-Ho-ho-ho!

00:15:56.802 --> 00:15:58.979
-Somebody's gonna have
to board their ship!
-You know it!

00:16:00.589 --> 00:16:01.764
Intruders beaming in!

00:16:01.807 --> 00:16:04.027
Very slowly beaming in.

00:16:04.071 --> 00:16:05.594
We've got to go!

00:16:10.077 --> 00:16:11.817
We have to get to the armory!

00:16:11.861 --> 00:16:14.037
Looks like we'll have to repel
them the old-fashioned way.

00:16:14.081 --> 00:16:17.736
Setting my fists to stun
and my kicks to kill.

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:19.129
[grunts]

00:16:20.652 --> 00:16:23.829
Uh, guys, right here. Yep.
Great stuff in that one.

00:16:23.873 --> 00:16:27.050
-All the way in back there?
-How much contraband
have you hidden on my ship?

00:16:27.094 --> 00:16:28.791
I don't know. A lot.

00:16:28.834 --> 00:16:30.923
♪

00:16:34.188 --> 00:16:35.928
[shouting]

00:16:37.582 --> 00:16:39.584
[grunting]

00:16:40.977 --> 00:16:41.978
Side roll. Side roll.

00:16:42.022 --> 00:16:43.110
Double hand punch!

00:16:43.153 --> 00:16:44.850
[grunting]

00:16:44.894 --> 00:16:46.896
[shouts]

00:16:46.939 --> 00:16:48.811
-Pakled!
-Mariner,
in case we don't make it...

00:16:48.854 --> 00:16:49.899
We're making it.

00:16:49.942 --> 00:16:51.161
I wasn't mad
that you were stealing

00:16:51.205 --> 00:16:52.206
the &lt;i&gt;Sacramento&lt;/i&gt;promotion.

00:16:52.249 --> 00:16:53.511
I apply for those all the time.

00:16:53.555 --> 00:16:54.904
-Nothing ever comes of it.
-[groans]

00:16:54.947 --> 00:16:56.862
-What? Then why were
you freaking out?
-[grunts]

00:16:56.906 --> 00:16:59.039
Because you &lt;i&gt;would&lt;/i&gt;have gotten
it. And I'd-I'd miss you, okay?

00:16:59.082 --> 00:17:01.606
-You're my best friend.
-Oh, haven't you shared
enough secrets today?

00:17:01.650 --> 00:17:03.130
Just shut up!

00:17:03.173 --> 00:17:04.870
-[Freeman grunting]
-Pakled!

00:17:04.914 --> 00:17:06.611
[groaning]

00:17:06.655 --> 00:17:08.570
[cackling]

00:17:08.613 --> 00:17:10.311
[grunts]
Mom!

00:17:16.882 --> 00:17:18.841
Ransom, get our backs!

00:17:18.884 --> 00:17:19.972
Way ahead of you!
[grunts]

00:17:20.016 --> 00:17:21.017
My head!

00:17:22.149 --> 00:17:23.889
[yowls, clears threat]
Sorry.

00:17:23.933 --> 00:17:25.978
I mean get the captain
to the biobed, quick, quick!

00:17:26.022 --> 00:17:28.024
[groans]
Did we save the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos?&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:28.068 --> 00:17:29.156
Working on it.

00:17:29.199 --> 00:17:31.114
Ooh, I got it.
One illegal virus.

00:17:31.158 --> 00:17:33.073
[singsongy]: But someone has
to take it to the ship.

00:17:33.116 --> 00:17:34.726
But who's small enough
to go undetected?

00:17:34.770 --> 00:17:36.250
Yeah, and who could survive
in space without a ship?

00:17:36.293 --> 00:17:38.252
Someone who can travel
with the program safely stored

00:17:38.295 --> 00:17:39.949
in her hard drive.
[gasps]

00:17:39.992 --> 00:17:41.255
ALL:
Peanut Hamper!

00:17:41.298 --> 00:17:42.604
You can load the code
into their ship

00:17:42.647 --> 00:17:43.648
using your robotic abilities.

00:17:43.692 --> 00:17:45.128
Oh, my gosh, Peanut Hamper,

00:17:45.172 --> 00:17:46.695
you're gonna save the day!

00:17:47.826 --> 00:17:49.698
Eh, I'm gonna pass.

00:17:49.741 --> 00:17:51.613
I-I'm sorry, what?

00:17:51.656 --> 00:17:53.136
All that stuff sounded
way too scary.

00:17:53.180 --> 00:17:54.529
What about
"the needs of the many"?

00:17:54.572 --> 00:17:56.270
I joined Starfleet
to piss off my dad,

00:17:56.313 --> 00:17:57.749
not to be a virus bomb.

00:17:57.793 --> 00:17:59.664
Peanut Hamper,
this is not cool!

00:17:59.708 --> 00:18:01.275
-We're all going to die!
-Peanut Hamper!

00:18:01.318 --> 00:18:03.146
There are so many lives
at stake!

00:18:03.190 --> 00:18:05.105
You know what? I'm just going
to beam myself out

00:18:05.148 --> 00:18:06.715
of this whole sitch.

00:18:06.758 --> 00:18:08.108
Sucks to be organic.

00:18:08.151 --> 00:18:11.111
Enjoy having all your guts
fly out or whatever!

00:18:11.154 --> 00:18:14.114
You know what?
Peanut Hamper is a stupid name!

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:20.163
-That little [bleep].
-[gasps]

00:18:20.207 --> 00:18:23.166
Oh, my gosh. I'm back! I just
clicked myself back to normal.

00:18:23.210 --> 00:18:25.037
Let me just upload this. Whoa!

00:18:25.081 --> 00:18:26.996
Ugh, feels like
an ice cream headache.

00:18:27.039 --> 00:18:28.911
[grunts] Okay. Now I just need
to get on that ship.

00:18:28.954 --> 00:18:30.565
Wait, no! I-It's too dangerous.

00:18:30.608 --> 00:18:31.957
You must be
in a heroic bravery mode

00:18:32.001 --> 00:18:33.698
or something.
Keep clicking your button.

00:18:33.742 --> 00:18:35.047
L-Let me click it.
Click-click your button.

00:18:35.091 --> 00:18:36.701
No, Tendi, this is normal me.

00:18:36.745 --> 00:18:38.790
-I've got this.
-And I've got you.

00:18:38.834 --> 00:18:41.184
Rutherford!

00:18:41.228 --> 00:18:42.925
[grunting]

00:18:46.102 --> 00:18:47.669
You know
I can run on my own.

00:18:47.712 --> 00:18:49.801
[both grunt]

00:18:51.629 --> 00:18:54.241
[exclaims, laughs]

00:18:56.286 --> 00:18:58.636
&lt;i&gt;-[Shaxs laughing]
-[Rutherford screaming]&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:00.247 --> 00:19:04.164
This is the best day of my life!

00:19:04.207 --> 00:19:06.949
-Eat this!
-No, no, no, no, no!

00:19:06.992 --> 00:19:08.994
[both panting]

00:19:12.259 --> 00:19:14.957
Linked up. Come on, come on.

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:17.177
-[grunting, laughs]
-[indistinct shouting]

00:19:20.702 --> 00:19:22.399
Virus downloaded.
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, y...

00:19:22.443 --> 00:19:24.053
Download slowing to a crawl?

00:19:24.096 --> 00:19:26.360
-Wait, why? &lt;i&gt;
-Sorry, but no virus&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:26.403 --> 00:19:28.710
&lt;i&gt;until after these guys kill you.&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:28.753 --> 00:19:30.929
-What? Why? &lt;i&gt;
-Because you snapped my neck!&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:30.973 --> 00:19:32.235
-What's the holdup?
-RUTHERFORD: Damn it, Badgey,

00:19:32.279 --> 00:19:34.324
we don't have time for this,
okay? Do it now!

00:19:34.368 --> 00:19:35.934
&lt;i&gt;You want me to disable
their systems?&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:35.978 --> 00:19:37.240
&lt;i&gt;Fine. I'll do it...&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:37.284 --> 00:19:38.894
&lt;i&gt;explosively!&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:38.937 --> 00:19:40.983
[gasps]
He's gonna blow us up!

00:19:41.026 --> 00:19:42.376
Not if I have something
to scream about it.

00:19:42.419 --> 00:19:44.465
[both grunting]

00:19:46.293 --> 00:19:49.165
&lt;i&gt;Stop it! He's mine!&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:51.123 --> 00:19:53.952
Hang in there, baby bear!

00:19:53.996 --> 00:19:56.477
[shouts]

00:19:57.869 --> 00:19:59.741
&lt;i&gt;[straining]&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:59.784 --> 00:20:02.396
&lt;i&gt;-Ah, there we go.
-[laughs]&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:07.009 --> 00:20:08.532
[alarm blaring]

00:20:08.576 --> 00:20:10.795
BOIMLER:
Ah, they did it!
They got clear of the blast.

00:20:10.839 --> 00:20:12.319
Bringing main power
back on line.

00:20:14.408 --> 00:20:15.974
All invaders have been...
[grunts]

00:20:16.018 --> 00:20:17.280
neutralized.

00:20:17.324 --> 00:20:19.804
&lt;i&gt;FREEMAN:
As soon as the engines&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:19.848 --> 00:20:21.458
&lt;i&gt;are back on line,
get us the hell out of here.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:21.502 --> 00:20:24.244
&lt;i&gt;And hey, don't get
too comfortable in my chair.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:24.287 --> 00:20:25.462
[chuckles]
Yes, sir.

00:20:25.506 --> 00:20:27.290
No, no, no, no,
there's more of them!

00:20:27.334 --> 00:20:28.726
[Boimler screams]

00:20:30.902 --> 00:20:33.253
&lt;i&gt;We have you now,&lt;/i&gt;Enterprise.

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:40.260
[metal creaking]

00:20:47.049 --> 00:20:48.833
[grunts]
All hands to escape pods.

00:20:48.877 --> 00:20:49.965
Prepare to abandon ship.

00:20:50.008 --> 00:20:51.619
Wait. Incoming ship?

00:20:53.708 --> 00:20:54.970
It's the &lt;i&gt;Titan!&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:00.932 --> 00:21:04.022
Oh, no! It's another &lt;i&gt;Enterprise.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:07.461 --> 00:21:10.681
Red alert! A Pakled party,
and I wasn't invited?

00:21:10.725 --> 00:21:12.727
&lt;i&gt;[exhales] It's about time
you showed up, Will.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:14.381
Mariner? This makes us even.

00:21:14.424 --> 00:21:15.947
&lt;i&gt;-[gasps] You know Riker?
-Yeah.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:15.991 --> 00:21:17.514
&lt;i&gt;Who do you think hooks me up
with all my contraband?&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:17.558 --> 00:21:20.038
&lt;i&gt;Dude is flush with Romulan ale, illeg...&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:20.082 --> 00:21:21.953
-I'm sorry, what was that?
-[chuckles]: Uh...

00:21:21.997 --> 00:21:24.521
We're still at red alert.
Target those ships and fire!

00:21:24.565 --> 00:21:26.828
We're talking about this later.

00:21:31.572 --> 00:21:33.269
&lt;i&gt;[Pakled groans]&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:33.313 --> 00:21:35.532
Make us go.

00:21:35.576 --> 00:21:38.013
&lt;i&gt;Go, guys, go!&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:38.056 --> 00:21:40.407
-BOIMLER: They're retreating!
Yes!
-[all cheering]

00:21:48.806 --> 00:21:50.808
♪

00:21:55.639 --> 00:21:57.380
&lt;i&gt;FREEMAN:
No, no,&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:57.424 --> 00:21:58.903
I don't want
any cosmetic changes

00:21:58.947 --> 00:22:00.557
-to the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.
-Are you sure?&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:00.601 --> 00:22:03.386
Because I could add some jazzy
reflective panels and big...

00:22:03.430 --> 00:22:05.388
No. I hate it
when a ship gets repaired

00:22:05.432 --> 00:22:07.956
and comes out looking
all &lt;i&gt;Sovereign-class.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:07.999 --> 00:22:10.915
I want her to look
almost like she usually does.

00:22:10.959 --> 00:22:12.917
&lt;i&gt;TENDI:
All right,&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:12.961 --> 00:22:14.441
we have a good one today.

00:22:14.484 --> 00:22:17.835
Chapter 79: fluidic systems
and how to reroute them.

00:22:17.879 --> 00:22:20.577
-[clears throat]-[groans] Fluidics are so messy.

00:22:20.621 --> 00:22:22.753
[gasps]
Rutherford, you're awake. Oh!

00:22:22.797 --> 00:22:24.581
-I knew you'd be okay!
-What?

00:22:24.625 --> 00:22:27.018
-What happened?
-You saved the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos!&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:27.062 --> 00:22:29.412
Oh, I did? Wow!
That's pretty cool.

00:22:29.456 --> 00:22:31.414
-Are you my nurse?
-Nurse? [laughs]

00:22:31.458 --> 00:22:33.503
No, they just have been
giving me time off

00:22:33.547 --> 00:22:34.591
so I could sit with you.

00:22:34.635 --> 00:22:35.940
Oh, sweet. Nice to meet you.

00:22:35.984 --> 00:22:37.028
I'm Rutherford.

00:22:37.072 --> 00:22:39.770
Oh, your implant.

00:22:39.814 --> 00:22:42.599
I-It must have damaged
your long-term memory.

00:22:42.643 --> 00:22:44.514
Do you remember me at all?

00:22:44.558 --> 00:22:46.603
Well, no.
But don't take it personally.

00:22:46.647 --> 00:22:48.344
I don't remember
what I don't remember.

00:22:48.388 --> 00:22:49.737
[crying]

00:22:49.780 --> 00:22:52.566
You know what this means, right?

00:22:52.609 --> 00:22:55.830
We get to become best friends
all over again!

00:22:55.873 --> 00:22:57.005
Okeydokey.

00:22:57.048 --> 00:22:59.050
♪

00:23:00.138 --> 00:23:03.098
We'll never forget
Lieutenant Shaxs' sacrifice.

00:23:03.141 --> 00:23:06.014
He's with the Prophets now.

00:23:11.019 --> 00:23:13.848
[sighs]
I can't even begin to imagine

00:23:13.891 --> 00:23:15.806
-how I'm going to replace him.
-Well,

00:23:15.850 --> 00:23:18.374
wherever he is, I'm sure
he's full-throat screaming

00:23:18.418 --> 00:23:20.637
in someone's face
and ejecting a warp core.

00:23:20.681 --> 00:23:22.639
I'd like to think you're right.

00:23:22.683 --> 00:23:24.554
Ensign Beckett Mariner,

00:23:24.598 --> 00:23:26.469
beamed down to Beta III
without authorization.

00:23:26.513 --> 00:23:27.775
Oh, what, seriously?

00:23:27.818 --> 00:23:29.429
Contraband hidden
throughout the ship.

00:23:29.472 --> 00:23:32.040
Illegal weapons,
illicit drugs, a tribble?

00:23:32.083 --> 00:23:33.476
Yeah. That's for personal use.

00:23:33.520 --> 00:23:34.825
I've got a whole year's worth

00:23:34.869 --> 00:23:36.784
of your insubordinations
right here.

00:23:36.827 --> 00:23:38.655
Well, without
those "insubordinations,"

00:23:38.699 --> 00:23:41.005
-we'd all be dead right now.
-I know.

00:23:41.049 --> 00:23:45.009
Did you know Starfleet considersBeta III a known culture?

00:23:45.053 --> 00:23:47.142
They had no idea
the Betans had regressed.

00:23:47.185 --> 00:23:48.752
And the Pakleds? Well,

00:23:48.796 --> 00:23:51.059
the Pakleds murdered
the entire crew of the &lt;i&gt;Solvang&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:51.102 --> 00:23:53.627
because everyone assumed
they were a joke.

00:23:53.670 --> 00:23:54.889
Yeah, well, that's Starfleet.

00:23:54.932 --> 00:23:56.673
Good at observing
and bad at maintaining.

00:23:56.717 --> 00:23:59.023
You know, we can't just assume
people are gonna keep doing

00:23:59.067 --> 00:24:00.982
the right thing
a generation down the road.

00:24:01.025 --> 00:24:03.724
I agree. But as captain,

00:24:03.767 --> 00:24:06.596
I can't ignore protocol.
I'd lose my command.

00:24:06.640 --> 00:24:08.163
You, on the other hand...

00:24:08.206 --> 00:24:10.992
You see a problem,
you can solve it.

00:24:11.035 --> 00:24:13.560
Wait, are you saying
work together for a change?

00:24:13.603 --> 00:24:16.127
Might be useful to have a
captain on your side, you know?

00:24:16.171 --> 00:24:19.000
Instead of up your ass.
What do you say?

00:24:19.043 --> 00:24:21.698
Uh, I think we're both
getting thrown in the brig.

00:24:21.742 --> 00:24:24.571
[chuckles]
Let's not tell your father.

00:24:31.969 --> 00:24:34.058
Oh, that's Mariner.
We work with her. Mariner!

00:24:34.102 --> 00:24:36.539
-Over here! Hi.
-[grunts] Carol.

00:24:36.583 --> 00:24:38.541
I guess those &lt;i&gt;Cali&lt;/i&gt;class ships

00:24:38.585 --> 00:24:40.108
can hold their own
longer than people say.

00:24:40.151 --> 00:24:42.110
[chuckles]
Thanks for the assist, Captain.

00:24:42.153 --> 00:24:44.808
No need to be so formal.
You know, I was her mentor.

00:24:44.852 --> 00:24:46.549
Uh, yeah, well,
I remember it differently.

00:24:46.593 --> 00:24:48.769
You were sort of my cha'DIch.

00:24:48.812 --> 00:24:50.553
We used to get
in so much trouble.

00:24:50.597 --> 00:24:52.512
-FREEMAN: "We"?
-[chuckles]: Deanna,

00:24:52.555 --> 00:24:55.558
can you introduce meto any of your Betazoid friends?

00:24:55.602 --> 00:24:57.734
Jack, I sense
you exaggerate your confidence

00:24:57.778 --> 00:25:00.781
in order to mask
an ocean of insecurity.

00:25:00.824 --> 00:25:03.566
Oh! Will they sense that, too?
I can make that work for me.

00:25:03.610 --> 00:25:05.960
Wait, wait, wait, wait,
you made a dog?

00:25:06.003 --> 00:25:07.962
Yeah, and it could fly.
Ooh, ooh, ooh!

00:25:08.005 --> 00:25:09.746
And another time,
we stole bunch of T-88s.

00:25:09.790 --> 00:25:11.922
Aw, man! The scanners
with the purple stripe?

00:25:11.966 --> 00:25:13.837
Those are amazing.
What else did we do?

00:25:13.881 --> 00:25:15.796
I just wanted to say,
I was wrong.

00:25:15.839 --> 00:25:17.537
I'm glad
we followed our guts today.

00:25:17.580 --> 00:25:18.886
You &lt;i&gt;are&lt;/i&gt;my mentor.

00:25:18.929 --> 00:25:20.627
[coughs]
Whatever, nerd. Come on,

00:25:20.670 --> 00:25:22.585
we can hang
without me being your mentor.

00:25:22.629 --> 00:25:24.195
-I thought you wanted that.
-Eh, my target kind of moves.

00:25:24.239 --> 00:25:27.111
Well, from now on, no more
being obsessed with rank.

00:25:27.155 --> 00:25:29.766
Time to start appreciating
what I have right here.

00:25:29.810 --> 00:25:31.768
Hey, you know what?
I like this new Boimler.

00:25:31.812 --> 00:25:34.728
Good work today, Boomler. Ransomsays you're one of his best.

00:25:34.771 --> 00:25:37.121
-[leg thuds]
-Thank you, Captain Riker, sir!

00:25:37.165 --> 00:25:38.601
Hey, how about
you buy me a drink?

00:25:38.645 --> 00:25:40.168
You know, since we're even?
Remember?

00:25:40.211 --> 00:25:41.952
The thing with the aliens
where I saved your ass?

00:25:41.996 --> 00:25:43.650
MARINER:
We are not even,
and we don't use money.

00:25:43.693 --> 00:25:46.609
What's happened to you, man?
You used to be sharp.

00:25:46.653 --> 00:25:48.611
&lt;i&gt;Boimler, you backstabbing little weasel!&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:48.655 --> 00:25:50.787
&lt;i&gt;Yeah, next time I see you, I'm gonna kick your [bleep] ass.&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:50.831 --> 00:25:52.789
&lt;i&gt;I cannot believe
that you took a promotion&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:52.833 --> 00:25:55.618
&lt;i&gt;to the mother[bleep]&lt;/i&gt;Titan! &lt;i&gt;
Call me.&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:55.662 --> 00:25:57.141
Hey, Brad. We got to scoot.
[chuckles]

00:25:57.185 --> 00:25:58.882
So get your boots
and strap 'em up,

00:25:58.926 --> 00:26:00.101
'cause the captain wants us

00:26:00.144 --> 00:26:02.103
to escort Commander Troi
to Tulgana IV.

00:26:02.146 --> 00:26:03.757
Ooh, I hear
the Klingon district's intense.

00:26:03.800 --> 00:26:06.063
There's a bar in Andoria Town
you guys would love.

00:26:06.107 --> 00:26:07.804
Whoa, you've been there?

00:26:07.848 --> 00:26:09.284
Yeah. I can show you around
if you want.

00:26:09.327 --> 00:26:11.721
Dude, your PADD is blowing up.
Who is messaging you?

00:26:11.765 --> 00:26:13.636
She's just an old friend.
She kind of got mad

00:26:13.680 --> 00:26:15.856
when I took the promotion here.
Eh, she'll get over it.

00:26:15.899 --> 00:26:17.988
&lt;i&gt;MARINER:
Boimler! You can't &lt;i&gt;
keep ducking me forever.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:18.032 --> 00:26:19.642
It is a really small galaxy
out there.

00:26:19.686 --> 00:26:21.731
Sooner or later, I'm gonna runinto you, and I'm gonna feed you

00:26:21.775 --> 00:26:24.342
-to an Armus! You hear me?-JEN: Hey, psycho, keep it down.

00:26:24.386 --> 00:26:26.040
&lt;i&gt;-We're trying to sleep.
-MARINER: Oh, shut up, Jen.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:27.868 --> 00:26:29.652
I'm sorry I'm late.

00:26:29.696 --> 00:26:30.958
I was watching
the first &lt;i&gt;Enterprise&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:31.001 --> 00:26:32.568
on the holodeck.You know, Archer and those guys?

00:26:32.612 --> 00:26:34.744
What a story.
Those guys had a long road

00:26:34.788 --> 00:26:36.006
getting from there to here.

00:26:36.050 --> 00:26:37.660
Course setfor the Tulgana system, Captain.

00:26:37.704 --> 00:26:38.661
Awaiting your command.

00:26:38.705 --> 00:26:40.358
Ah, Tulgana IV.

00:26:40.402 --> 00:26:42.273
You know,
they have a Little Risa.

00:26:42.317 --> 00:26:44.841
Oh, so then should we take
the little horga'hn?

00:26:44.885 --> 00:26:46.800
No. Let's take
the one we always use.

00:26:46.843 --> 00:26:48.758
-[clears throat]
-Right. Give me warp

00:26:48.802 --> 00:26:51.369
in the factor
of five, six, seven, eight.

00:26:51.413 --> 00:26:53.676
&lt;i&gt;TROI:
Oh, the jazz.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:53.720 --> 00:26:55.722
♪

00:26:58.725 --> 00:27:01.249
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

00:27:01.292 --> 00:27:02.293
Help! Help!
